{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294","id":5088215665,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABL0gCcQ","number":294,"title":"Does the Section 3 narrowMatch pattern extend to source-material records?","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:11:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T08:11:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The Edison literature sweep surfaced two records whose reports identify a\nconfident ontology term while explicitly refusing to assert an identity mapping:\n\n| record | term | report's words |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Calf brains` | `UBERON:0000955` *brain* | \"high-confidence anatomical-source annotation\" but \"do **not** assert `skos:exactMatch` or `skos:closeMatch`\" |\n| `Cow manure` | `ENVO:00003031` *animal manure* | recommends retaining UNMAPPED |\n\nBoth terms resolve correctly against the local builds, and both prefixes are\nalready in `promote_resolved_unmapped.py`'s `ONTOLOGY_DB`.\n\nThe reports forbid `exactMatch` and `closeMatch` — the two predicates that\nlicense node substitution. They do not mention `skos:narrowMatch`, which is\nexactly the predicate that says the subject is *narrower than* the object\nwithout claiming they are interchangeable, and which MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md\nSection 3 already uses for hydrates (`NaH2PO4*H2O` narrowMatch the anhydrous\n`CHEBI:37585`).\n\nSo the question is a policy one, not a lookup one: **is Section 3's\nidentifier + narrowMatch + Rule B1 registry row pattern meant only for\nhydrate/salt variants of a parent compound, or does it also cover\nsource-qualified materials** — calf brains as a narrower thing than brain, cow\nmanure than animal manure, larchwood xylan than xylan?\n\nArguments each way:\n\n- **For extending it.** These records would gain a real, correct, non-substituting\n  edge into UBERON/ENVO, which is more than the current UNMAPPED conveys. The\n  narrowMatch semantics are literally true.\n- **Against.** \"Calf brains\" as a medium ingredient is a *preparation*, and\n  narrowMatch on a preparation-to-anatomy axis is a different relation from\n  narrowMatch on a hydrate-to-anhydrous axis. Conflating them makes the\n  predicate mean two things, and kg-microbe consumers cannot tell which.\n  UBERON:0000955 as an *anatomical source* — which is what the report actually\n  recommends — is arguably a schema slot, not an SSSOM row.\n\nNothing was applied; the records stay UNMAPPED and the CURIEs are recorded in\ntheir curation history. Raising this because the same question governs a\nrecurring class of records (extracts, tissue preparations, source-qualified\npolymers), and deciding it once is better than deciding it per record.\n\nBlocked on a curator's call; see also #236 on subject/file identity.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/294/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}